[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 377,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 176,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57117,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 176,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>A hamartoma is a well-demarcated, generally encapsulated mass composed of normal breast tissue components.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-06-19T15:30:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 378,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 177,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57118,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 177,
        "headingText": "<p>None</p>",
        "timestamp": "2019-08-28T10:37:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 379,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 178,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57119,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 178,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-06-19T15:30:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 380,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 179,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57120,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 179,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> adenolipoma; chondrolipoma; myoid hamartoma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> fibroadenolipoma; adenolipofibroma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-06-19T15:30:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 381,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 180,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57121,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 180,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-06-19T15:30:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 382,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 181,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57122,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 181,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There is no predilection for any breast quadrant for the development of hamartoma {12121234}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-06-19T15:30:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 383,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 182,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57123,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 182,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Hamartomas may present as soft palpable masses {12121234; 12461066} or are asymptomatic and detected by mammography {7785651; 11328316}. Imaging shows circumscribed rounded masses, sometimes with intralesional heterogeneous echogenicity on ultrasonography {8996902}. Owing to their well-defined borders, hamartomas are easily enucleated. Most hamartomas are sporadic; multiple hamartomas can be seen in Cowden syndrome {9445133}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-06-19T15:30:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 384,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 183,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57124,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 183,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Hamartomas account for &lt;&nbsp;5% of benign breast tumours {8078805; 25141109}, occurring predominantly in women in their fifth decade of life (ranging from 33.5 to 66.5&nbsp;years) {25141109}, although they can be found at any age.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-06-19T15:30:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 385,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 184,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57125,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 184,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most hamartomas are sporadic, and the etiology is largely unclear, although weak evidence suggests hormonal influences {10337660; 12121234}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-06-19T15:30:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 386,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 185,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57126,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 185,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Because some hamartomas are associated with molecular changes, different perspectives exist as to whether they are neoplasms or malformations. Genetic data are limited, but aberrations involving chromosomal regions 12q12-q15 and 6p21, as well as PTEN loss, have been described {9290959; 7497449; 8143274}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-06-19T15:30:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 393,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 206,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57127,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 206,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Hamartomas are round or oval, measuring as much as 20&nbsp;cm in diameter. The cut surface may resemble normal breast tissue, lipoma, or fibroadenoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-06-19T15:30:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 387,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 186,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57128,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 186,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Generally encapsulated, hamartomas are lobulated and show ducts, lobules, and adipose tissue in varying proportions. Commonly there is prominent intralobular fibrosis, and the lobules have an atrophic appearance. Adipocytes may occur singly, and they are encased by dense fibrous tissue (encapsulated fat). Hamartomas may be called adenolipomas when features of normal ducts/lobules are mixed with adipose tissue {1866672}, myoid hamartomas when a smooth muscle component is prominent {3972402}, and chondrolipomas when chondroid islands exist within adipose tissue {2669070}. When only limited material is available, as with core biopsy, the diagnosis may be suggested by taking into consideration the radiological and clinical findings {12461066}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-06-19T15:30:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 388,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 187,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57129,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 187,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The epithelial and stromal components of hamartomas show bland cytology. Cytological diagnosis is frequently limited by scant material and features overlapping with those of other benign lesions {12461066; 12925988}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-06-19T15:30:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 389,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 188,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57130,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 188,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-06-19T15:30:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 392,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 191,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57131,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 191,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a mass lesion comprising components of normal breast tissue; correlation is required with clinical and imaging features.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-06-19T15:30:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 390,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 189,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57132,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 189,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-06-19T15:30:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 391,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 190,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57133,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 50,
        "headingId": 190,
        "headingText": "<p>Hamartomas rarely recur. Reported recurrences probably represent incompletely excised lesions {7785651; 19624414}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2019-10-11T11:58:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]